# =============================================================================
# What must NOT be copied into the Docker build context.
#
# The first rule is the one that matters. On CI the local configuration is absent
# (it is git-ignored), but a developer building this image on their own machine has
# a real application-dev.properties on disk holding the database password, the
# Cognito client secret and an AWS key. Without this file, "COPY src ./src" would
# bake all three into an image that then gets pushed to a registry.
#
# Configuration reaches the container through environment variables at run time,
# never through the image.
# =============================================================================

# The DEV configuration only — it is the one holding real credentials.
#
# application.properties and application-prod.properties are deliberately NOT excluded:
# they carry no secrets, and the production image needs them if they are present at
# build time. (In CI they are absent anyway — all three are git-ignored — so the image
# ships with no configuration and every setting must arrive as an environment variable.
# See RegulaOne/docs/backend-configuration.md.)
src/main/resources/application-dev.properties*

# Build output — the image compiles from source, so a host build is not reused
target/

# Tooling and local noise
.mvn/
mvnw
mvnw.cmd
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store
HELP.md
